search_informal_description:
The closure of the parameter set $\text{paramSet}(K)$ for the fundamental cone of a number field $K$ is equal to the product over all infinite places $w$ of $K$ of the closed interval $(-\infty, 0]$ if $w$ is the distinguished place $w_0$, and the closed interval $[0,1]$ otherwise. That is,
$$
\text{closure}(\text{paramSet}(K)) = \prod_{w \in \text{InfinitePlace}(K)} \begin{cases}
(-\infty, 0] & \text{if } w = w_0, \\
[0,1] & \text{otherwise.}
\end{cases}
$$

