The real number defined as the infinite sum
\[
\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}
\frac{(-1)^k\,(6k)!\,(13591409+545140134\,k)}{(3k)!\,(k!)^3\,(640320)^{3k+\frac32}}
\]
which appears in Chudnovsky’s formula for $1/\pi$.

informal_statement:
Compute

$$
\lim _{h \rightarrow 0} \frac{\sin \left(\frac{\pi}{3}+4 h\right)-4 \sin \left(\frac{\pi}{3}+3 h\right)+6 \sin \left(\frac{\pi}{3}+2 h\right)-4 \sin \left(\frac{\pi}{3}+h\right)+\sin \left(\frac{\pi}{3}\right)}{h^{4}}
$$
 Prove that the answer is: \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2}

Over all pairs of complex numbers $(x, y)$ satisfying the equations

$$
x+2 y^{2}=x^{4} \quad \text { and } \quad y+2 x^{2}=y^{4}
$$

compute the minimum possible real part of $x$.
 Prove that the answer is: -\frac{1+\sqrt{5}}{2}

Let $ a, b \in \mathbb{N}$  with $ 1 \leq a \leq b,$ and $ M \equal{} \left[\frac {a \plus{} b}{2} \right].$ Define a function $ f: \mathbb{Z} \mapsto \mathbb{Z}$ by
\[ f(n) \equal{} \begin{cases} n \plus{} a, & \text{if } n \leq M, \\
n \minus{} b, & \text{if } n >M. \end{cases}
\]
Let $ f^1(n) \equal{} f(n),$ $ f_{i \plus{} 1}(n) \equal{} f(f^i(n)),$ $ i \equal{} 1, 2, \ldots$ Find the smallest natural number $ k$ such that $ f^k(0) \equal{} 0.$
 Prove that the answer is: \frac {a + b}{\gcd(a,b)}

