\begin{align*}
\|f'(t) - v(t, f(t))\| &\leq \varepsilon_f, \\
\|g'(t) - v(t, g(t))\| &\leq \varepsilon_g,
\end{align*}
for all $t \in [a, b)$. If the initial distance satisfies $\|f(a) - g(a)\| \leq \delta$, then for all $t \in [a, b]$, the distance between $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ is bounded by:
\[ \|f(t) - g(t)\| \leq \text{gronwallBound}(\delta, K, \varepsilon_f + \varepsilon_g, t - a), \]
where
\[ \text{gronwallBound}(\delta, K, \varepsilon, t) = 
\begin{cases} 
\delta + \varepsilon t & \text{if } K = 0, \\
\delta e^{K t} + \frac{\varepsilon}{K}(e^{K t} - 1) & \text{if } K \neq 0.
\end{cases} \]

