Let \(k(\geqslant 2)\) be a given positive integer. For any \(1\leqslant i\leqslant k\), the numbers \(a_i\) and \(d_i\) are positive integers. The arithmetic sequence \(\{a_i + nd_i\}\) (\(n = 0,1,2,\cdots\)) corresponds to the set \(A_i=\{a_i+nd_i\mid n = 0,1,2,\cdots\}\), where \(1\leqslant i\leqslant k\). It is known that \(A_1,A_2,\cdots,A_k\) form a \(k -\)partition of \(\mathbf{N}^*\) (that is, the intersections of \(A_1,\cdots,A_k\) taken pairwise are empty sets, and \(A_1\cup\cdots\cup A_k=\mathbf{N}^*\)). Prove the following conclusions:

(1) \(\frac{1}{d_1}+\cdots+\frac{1}{d_k}=1\);

(2) \(\frac{a_1}{d_1}+\cdots+\frac{a_k}{d_k}=\frac{k + 1}{2}\).

